Virtio-net bringup (x86_64)
============================

One-shot probe + init helper, kicked off from `kernel_main`
before RS starts. Logs the MAC (or a fail-code) to the serial
console, same shape as the aarch64 equivalent in
`board/virt/hello.lsysl`.

Lives in `oskit.drivers.virtio` — the bringup is a thin helper
that *uses* virtio_net, so it belongs with the virtio driver
(arch-code depending on drivers is the wrong direction and
creates an import cycle with `virtio_transport_pci.lsysl`).
x86-specific only because it talks to the COM1 UART via
`oskit.arch.x86_64.uart_puts`.

    module oskit.drivers.virtio

    import oskit.arch.x86_64.{uart_puts, uart_putc}


Render `v` as two hex nibbles (no 0x prefix) to the UART.

    vb_put_byte_hex(v: int)
        val hi = (v >> 4) & 0xF
        val lo = v & 0xF
        if hi < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + hi)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + hi - 10)
        if lo < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + lo)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + lo - 10)


One-nibble renderer for the fail-code.

    vb_put_nibble(v: int)
        if v < 10
            uart_putc(int('0') + v)
        else
            uart_putc(int('a') + v - 10)


Probe + init virtio-net. On failure, log a small numeric code
from `virtio_net_last_fail` (1=not found, 2=no VERSION_1,
3=FEATURES_OK rejected, 4=RX queue setup, 5=TX queue setup).
On success, log the negotiated MAC.

Must run before any networking code depends on `virtio_net_send`
/ `virtio_net_recv`.

    virtio_net_bringup()
        if virtio_net_init() == 0
            uart_puts("virtio-net: init failed, code=")
            vb_put_nibble(virtio_net_last_fail())
            uart_puts("\n")
            return
        var mac: [6]byte
        if virtio_net_get_mac(mac) != 0
            uart_puts("virtio-net: MAC=")
            var i = 0
            while i < 6
                vb_put_byte_hex(int(mac[i]) & 0xff)
                if i < 5
                    uart_putc(int(':'))
                i += 1
            uart_puts("\n")
        else
            uart_puts("virtio-net: no MAC configured\n")
